A developer wants to copy every element of arr into first, but the final element is missing. Which line is the bug?
const arr = [10, 20, 30];
const first = arr.slice(0, arr.length - 1);
console.log(first);
const tail = arr[arr.length - 1];

This arrow function is supposed to return twice its argument, but every call yields undefined. Which line is the bug?
const double = x => { x * 2; };
const y = double(5);
console.log(y);
let z = 0;

A queue helper must add item to the FRONT of list, but the item keeps landing at the back. Which line is the bug?
function addItem(list, item) {
  list.push(item);
  return list;
}
const out = addItem([1], 2);

This async function should return the parsed JSON from an endpoint, but it returns a pending promise's json method chain incorrectly. Which line is the bug?
async function getData() {
  const result = fetch('/api');
  return result.json();
}
const data = await getData();

A value is compared to the number 5, but strings like '5' are incorrectly treated as a match. Which line is the bug?
if (value == 5) {
  return undefined;
}
return value;
}

Inside a block the code declares name, yet the very next line outside that block can still read it. Which line is the bug?
{
  var name = "test";
}
console.log(name);
return name;
